<title>SINGAPORE: Asian rice prices - April 3.</title>
<headline>Asian rice prices - April 3.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted on Thursday by trading and official sources in the key Asian producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, Pakistan and India in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     April 3  March 27</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 330-350   340-375</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok     670-690   680-690</p>
<p>India-5.0 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB  310     300-305</p>
<p>India-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  290     280-285</p>
<p>India-15 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  260     250-255</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  245     235-245</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port     250-260     255</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	240-250     245</p>
<p>Pakistan-Basmati super FOB Pakistan port	 580-595   595-605</p>
<p>Pakistan-IRRI 6 FOB Pakistan port		  220-225   225-235</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
